---

## 10. Recommended thesis framing (what the proposal now claims)

> **"Lifecycle-Efficient Adaptive Edge AI: Reversibility-Enabled Drift-Triggered Selective
> Model Updates on Microcontroller-Class Devices"**

Four verified "firsts":
1. First reversible-layer on-device learning on MCU-class hardware (activation-free
   backprop; answers DaCapo via BDIA-style exact reversibility with unchanged inference architecture)
2. First drift-triggered selective block updates with built-in rollback on MCUs
   (SEKF = server, Minerva = full-model, SoLA = LLMs)
3. First serverless fleet coordination of selective updates under heterogeneous drift with
   lifecycle-energy objective (DriftGuard = centralized; surveys demand drift-aware aggregation)
4. First standardized lifecycle evaluation with explicit power/latency budgets on real
   hardware (E2R/T2R/SS; every survey calls for it)

Flagship application: **sensor calibration and predictive maintenance on IIoT** — the only
real-world drift-regime application in the ODL literature, and a natural match for Soham's
production anomaly-detection instincts.

Stretch (optional, high reward): **batteryless/intermittent devices + reversibility** — no
checkpoints needed when activations are reconstructible.

